{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ובני ישראל נסעו מבארות בני יעקן מוסרה שם מת אהרן", :translit "uvnei yisra'el nas'u mibe'erot benei ya'akan moserah sham met aharon", :gloss "and the children of Israel journeyed from Beeroth Bene-jaakan to Moserah there died Aaron"} {:he "קשה מיתת הצדיקים כשבירת הלוחות", :translit "kasheh mitat ha-tzadikim kishbirat ha-luchot", :gloss "difficult is the death of the righteous like the breaking of the tablets"} {:he "ת\"ח שמת הכל נעשין קרוביו", :translit "t\"ch she-met ha-kol na'asin krovav", :gloss "a Torah scholar who died everyone becomes his relatives"} {:he "צריכין לקרוע עליו כמו על ספר תורה שנשרף", :translit "tzrichin likroa alav kemo al sefer torah shenisraf", :gloss "they must tear over him like over a Torah scroll that was burned"} {:he "ואשים הלוחות בארון", :translit "va'asim ha-luchot ba'aron", :gloss "and I placed the tablets in the ark"} {:he "ס\"ת שבלה קוברין אותה אצל תלמיד חכם", :translit "s\"t shebaleh kovrin otah etzel talmid chacham", :gloss "a Torah scroll that wore out they bury it next to a Torah scholar"} {:he "קיים זה מה שכתוב בזה", :translit "kiyam zeh mah shekatuv bazeh", :gloss "this one fulfilled what is written in that one"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition (semikhut): death of Aaron placed near breaking of tablets and near placing tablets in ark"}], :frame {:text "The Talmud states that the death of the righteous is as difficult before the Holy One as the day the tablets were broken (Shabbat 105a; Mo'ed Katan 25a). The Talmud also teaches that upon the death of a Torah scholar, all Jews are considered his relatives for the obligation of keriah, and one tears for him as one tears for a burned Torah scroll (Mo'ed Katan 25a). The Mishnah rules that a worn-out Torah scroll is buried next to a Torah scholar, for 'this one fulfilled what is written in that one' (Megillah 3b, 26b).", :sources ["Shabbat 105a" "Mo'ed Katan 25a" "Megillah 26b"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ויקבר", :translit "vayikavor", :gloss "and he buried"} {:he "ויכהן", :translit "vayikahen", :gloss "and he served as priest / and the priest"} {:he "מיתת צדיקים מכפרת כבגדי כהונה", :translit "mitat tzadikim mechaperet kibgdei kehunah", :gloss "the death of the righteous atones like the priestly garments"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Wordplay: ויקבר read as an allusion to ויכהן, linking burial of the righteous to priestly atonement"}], :frame {:text "The Talmud teaches that the death of the righteous atones, comparing it to the atoning function of the priestly garments: just as the priestly vestments atone, so the death of the righteous brings atonement (Zevachim 88b, citing the juxtaposition of garments and atonement in Leviticus 16:4).", :sources ["Zevachim 88b" "Leviticus 16:4"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition (semikhut): death of Aaron placed near breaking of tablets and near placing tablets in ark", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Wordplay: ויקבר read as an allusion to ויכהן, linking burial of the righteous to priestly atonement", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:35:39.964321467Z", :model "glm-5.2"}